    S:gt.blockmachines.multimachine.large-hadron-collider.tooltip=Machine Type: §eParticle Accelerator, Particle Collider, LHC§r\nAccelerates particles to high energies and then collides them to generate new particles\nElectrically neutral particles are unaffected\nSet the §9Target Beam Energy§7 (up to 2TeV) and the §dmaximum number of cycles§7\nCycles every second\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\n§f§nAccelerator mode§7\nAccelerates the beam in the smaller LHC ring\nAccelerator mode increases the §9Beam Energy§7 by §3EU Consumed in cycle§7 * §f0.1eV§7 / §6Beam Rate§7,\nuntil the §9Target Beam Energy§7 is reached, or the §dmaximum number of cycles§7 is reached\nIf the §9Target Beam Energy§7 is reached, add §f0.3§7 * §6Beam Rate§7 to the current §6Beam Rate§7\nHowever, if the current §6Beam Rate§7 >= §f5000§7, add (§f0.3§7 * §6Beam Rate§7)^§f0.5§7\nto the current §6Beam Rate§7 instead\n§3Power§7 cost starts at §f1A§7 of §fUV§7 per §6Beam Rate§7 and increases quadratically\nwith the §dnumber of completed cycles§7\n§3P§7 = (§f1A UV§7) * §6R§7 * (§dN§7+1)^2\nAutomatically switches to Collider mode when the §dmaximum number of cycles§7 is reached\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\n§f§nCollider mode§7\nSplits the beam into §ftwo§7 beams that go in opposite directions in the larger LHC ring, which\nthen collide to generate new particles\nThe §bCollision Energy§7 is two times the §9Beam Energy§7\nIf the §bCollision Energy§7 exceeds the rest mass of a particle, that particle will start\nappearing in the outputs\nA particle output can only appear in the modules that correspond to the forces that\ninteract with that particle\nFor example, Neutrinos cannot appear in the Strong force module, §fALICE§7, since they do\nnot interact via the strong force\n§fFiltered Beam Output Hatches§7 will allow you to see the list of possible outputs, and\nfilter them\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nThere are four LHC modules, marked by the letter on top of the module:\n§bE - Electromagnetism§7 - Charged Matter Sensor (§bCMS§7)\n§2W - Weak Interaction§7 - Advanced Total Lepton Assimilation Snare (§2ATLAS§7)\n§fS - Strong Force§7 - Absolute Lattice Integrated Chromodynamic Encapsulator (§fALICE§7)\n§5G - Gravity§7 - Localized Horizon Curvature Binder (§5LHCb§7)\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\n§aSupports Multi-Amp and Laser Hatches!\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nHold §l[LSHIFT]§r§7 to display structure guidelines\nAdded by: §aAuthor: §6Ham§fCorp§r§7
    S:gt.blockmachines.multimachine.large-hadron-collider.tooltip_secondary=§fDimensions: §6122§7x§6109§7x§613§7 (§6L§7x§6W§7x§6H§7) §c(Hollow)\n§fStructure: \n   §fController: §7Front center of accelerator ring, 12th layer\n   §65664 §fCollider Casing\n   §673 §fNeonite (any color)\n   §620 §fShielded Accelerator Glass\n   §616 §fShielded Accelerator Casing\n   §e1 §fBeam Input Hatch: §7Entrance to accelerator ring\n   §e1+ §fEnergy Hatch: §7Any casing\n   \n   §bCMS Module §9(E)\n   §6523 §fCollider Casing\n   §6148 §fCharged Matter Sensor Casing\n   §6126 §fShielded Accelerator Glass\n   §611 §fNeonite (any color)\n   §e2 §fFiltered Beam Output Hatch: §7Inner side of module\n   \n   §bATLAS Module §9(W)\n   §6515 §fCollider Casing\n   §6160 §fAdvanced Total Lepton Assimilation Snare Casing\n   §6126 §fShielded Accelerator Glass\n   §613 §fNeonite (any color)\n   §e2 §fFiltered Beam Output Hatch: §7Inner side of module\n   \n   §bALICE Module §9(S)\n   §6517 §fCollider Casing\n   §6158 §fAbsolute Lattice Integrated Chromodynamic Encapsulator Casing\n   §6140 §fShielded Accelerator Glass\n   §611 §fNeonite (any color)\n   §e2 §fFiltered Beam Output Hatch: §7Inner side of module\n   \n   §bLHCb Module §9(G)\n   §6511 §fCollider Casing\n   §6144 §fLocalized Horizon Curvature Binder Casing\n   §6126 §fShielded Accelerator Glass\n   §617 §fNeonite (any color)\n   §e2 §fFiltered Beam Output Hatch: §7Inner side of module\n   \nProjector stack size determines §bNumber of Modules\n§7§m------------------------------\n§fUse the Multiblock Structure §9Hologram §1Projector§f to visualize/build the structure!
    S:gt.blockmachines.multimachine.large-neutralization-engine.name=Large Neutralization Engine
    S:gt.blockmachines.multimachine.large-neutralization-engine.tooltip=기계 종류: §e산(Acid) 생성기, LNE§r\n(모든 문제를) 녹여드립니다!\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\n§b염기§7를 사용하여 §d효율§7을 높일 수 있습니다 (하나씩 소모됨):\n§b수산화나트륨§7 : §d150%§7 : §f60§7/분\n§b수산화칼륨§7 : §d190%§7 : §f24§7/분\n§b수산화세슘§7 : §d250%§7 : §f6§7/분\n§b수산화프랑슘§7 : §d500%§7 : §f5§7/분\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\n산을 태워 §c독성 잔여물§7을 생성합니다\n§c독성 잔여물§7이 §3용량§7을 초과하면 멀티블록이 §4폭발합니다!\n매 §f틱§7마다 §c독성 잔여물§7은 §6잔여물 비율§7*§e연료 소비량(L)§7*rand(§f0.7§7,§f1.3§7)만큼 §f증가§7합니다\n§6잔여물 비율§7은 §f0.05§7*§d기본 연료 가치 (EU/L)§7^§f0.8로 계산됩니다\n매 §f틱§7마다 §c독성 잔여물§7은 §9기본 붕괴§7*§e붕괴 증폭§7*(§c독성 잔여물§7^§f0.08§7)만큼 §f감소§7합니다\n멀티블록이 비활성화되면 잔여물 붕괴 속도가 §f10§7배 느려집니다\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\n§d로봇 팔§7을 넣어 §e붕괴 증폭§7을 높일 수 있습니다:\n§e붕괴 증폭§7은 §f1.2§7^§d로봇 팔 티어§7 (§aIV§7 이하) 또는 §f1.4§7^§d로봇 팔 티어§7 (§dLuV§7 이상)로 계산됩니다\n§d여러 개§7(§f16§7개 최대)의 로봇 팔을 넣으면 §e붕괴 증폭§7에 sqrt(§d로봇 팔 개수§7)를 곱합니다\n매 §f분§7마다 §d로봇 팔 개수§7/(§f45§7*(§f1§7+§d로봇 팔 티어§7)) 확률로 사용된 로봇 팔 §f하나§7가 §c소멸§7합니다\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\n구조물에는 §f3티어§7가 있으며, §f티어§7에 따라 §9기본 붕괴§7와 §3용량§7이 결정됩니다:\n§fT1§7 : §f강화 무생명 기계 케이싱§7 : §9200§7 : §3375,000\n§fT2§7 : §f정밀 고정 기계 케이싱§7 : §9400§7 : §31,000,000\n§fT3§7 : §f궁극 정적 기계 케이싱§7 : §9700§7 : §32,500,000\n§a멀티앰프 및 레이저 해치 지원!\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\n§l[LSHIFT]§r§7를 누르고 있으면 구조 가이드라인을 표시합니다
